\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every $n\geq 2$ and every smooth Riemannian metric on the standard smooth sphere $S^{n}$, must there be infinitely many geometrically distinct prime closed geodesics? Geometric distinctness means different image sets; simplicity is not required.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every $n\geq 2$ and every smooth Riemannian metric on the standard smooth sphere $S^{n}$, must there be infinitely many geometrically distinct prime closed geodesics? Geometric distinctness means different image sets; simplicity is not required.

